{
  "_comment": "SEED DASHBOARD - hand-authored against the metric names shipped by tasks 1-8 of issue #239; a live SigNoz was not available to author/export against. Import it, drive one loadgenerator run, refine panels/units/queries in the SigNoz UI, then re-export over this file and re-commit. The JSON schema is SigNoz-version-coupled (authored for signoz v0.129.0) - re-export on a SigNoz bump. Some panels are latent until their Micrometer binder is enabled: the Persistence row needs quarkus.datasource.jdbc.enable-metrics=true and the Cache row needs quarkus.cache.caffeine.\"<name>\".metrics-enabled=true - neither is set today. See docs/observability.md.",
  "title": "Translatr - Load Test",
  "description": "Load-test observability for the Quarkus backend (OpenTelemetry + SigNoz, issue #239): throughput, latency percentiles, error rate, saturation, JVM runtime, DB pool, cache, and API-key usage. SEED DASHBOARD - hand-authored against the metric names shipped by tasks 1-8 of issue #239; a live SigNoz was not available to author/export against. Import it, drive one loadgenerator run, refine panels/units/queries in the SigNoz UI, then re-export over this file and re-commit. The JSON schema is SigNoz-version-coupled (authored for signoz v0.129.0) - re-export on a SigNoz bump. Some panels are latent until their Micrometer binder is enabled: the Persistence row needs quarkus.datasource.jdbc.enable-metrics=true and the Cache row needs quarkus.cache.caffeine.\"<name>\".metrics-enabled=true - neither is set today. See docs/observability.md.",
